  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\nGodan verb (intransitive). The transitive counterpart is {茹|ゆ}で{上|あ}げる (to finish boiling something). Part of the common ～{上|あ}がる pattern indicating completion of an action.\n\nUSAGE:\nPrimarily a cooking term. Sometimes written in hiragana as ゆで{上|あ}がる.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- パスタが{茹|ゆ}で{上|あ}がる: the pasta finishes boiling\n- {麺|めん}が{茹|ゆ}で{上|あ}がる: the noodles finish boiling\n- {卵|たまご}が{茹|ゆ}で{上|あ}がる: the eggs finish boiling",
